   "design": "With each worker's consent, interviews are recorded and a scribe drafts the note in the job analysis sections; the psychologist corrects every note. Workers fill in the satisfaction questionnaire online, which writes the data, instead of the psychologist typing paper forms. Corrected notes are coded against a fixed codebook, and the psychologist checks every coded passage. Planning, observation, interviews and follow-up stay with the psychologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Notes, questionnaires and coding were all done by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Consent-based scribes, online forms and codebook coding with quoted passages.",
   "still_hard": "Workers who will not speak openly on record.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing what a job really demands beyond what workers say.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less typing and first coding; observing and interviewing stay.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "workers",
     "task": "Describe their jobs",
     "learn": "Whether recording changes what they say."
    }
   ],
